NAME

ulibAddToFLOFile - Adds a line to a .FLO file


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibAddToFLOFile(struct FidoNetAddress *Fido, char *PacketName, long Force)
                                    a0                    a1              d0


DESCRIPTION

This function adds <PacketName> to the .FLO file of the FidoNet node contained
in <Fido>.

If the .FLO file does not already exist, one will be created.

It is possible that another node has a file lock on <PacketName>, in which case
this function would, under normal circumstances, fail.

The <Force> parameter, if set to a non-zero value, will cause this function to
wait until <PacketName> can be opened successfully.  It is recommended that
you use the <Force> parameter in your programs, just in case another program
happens to be accessing the .FLO file.

NOTE:  This function will report an error if <PacketName> is already present
       in the .FLO file.


RETURNS

0        - Success
Non-zero - Failure

              1 - File exists, but couldn't open for append
              2 - File does not exist, but couldn't open new file
              3 - <PacketName> is already in the .FLO file
